<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105530" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροπός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>twisted leathern thong,</i> with
			which the oar was fastened to the thole, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροποῖς ἐν δερματίνοισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.782
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				8.53
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροπὸν αὐτόν, ἐπαρτέα δεσμὸν ἐρετμοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					5.359
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροπόω</span> (B), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροπωτήρ.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
